                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There is zero relatable mahjong element except for the remotely vague-looking tiles.\nNo concentration needed. I played it perfectly sleep-deprived while listening to the ingame music\nThere is almost no puzzle-solving. All you need to do is click on two matching exposed or linked tiles. By any chance if you manage to reach a point where you can no longer make anymore moves, the reamining tiles reshuffle themselves to allow you to complete the round.\n\nNo replay value at all. Avoid..\n\n[h1] Only recommended for Idling cards [/h1]",
